hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"93","“Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) made a signet ring of silver, so it was in his possession. Then it was in the possession of Abu Bakr and the possession of 'Umar. Then it was in the possession of 'Uthman, until it fell into the well of Aris. Its engraved inscription was: ‘Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.”"
"94","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to wear his signet ring on his right hand.”"
"95","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to wear his signet ring on his right hand.”"
"96","\I saw Ibn Abi Rafi' wearing a signet ring on his right hand"","" so I asked him about that and he said: 'I saw 'Abdu llah ibn Ja'far wearing a signet ring on his right hand'"","" and 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far said:\n'Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to wear a signet ring on his right hand'.”"""""
"97","“He (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to wear a signet ring on his right hand.”"
"98","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to wear a signet ring on his right hand.”"""""
"99","“Ibn 'Abbas used to wear a signet ring on his right hand, without adornment, and he said: 'Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to wear a signet ring on his right hand'.”"
"100","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) chose a signet ring of silver"","" and put its stone in the part close to the\npalm of his hand. On it he engraved: “Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah"",""” and he forbade anyone [else] to engrave on it. It is the one that fell from Mu'aiqib into the well of Aris.”"""""
"101","\Al-Hasan and al-Husain used to wear signet rings on their left hands.\"""""""
